LIKH-naa"],["to sleep","sona","SOH-naa"],["to learn","seekhna","SEEKH-naa"],["to help","madad karna","MUH-dud KUR-naa"],["to need","zaroorat hona","za-ROO-rut HOH-naa"],["to love","pyaar karna","pyaar KUR-naa"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Hindi has no he / she difference in the pronoun for \"he, she, it\": vah. The verb shows the gender. aap is the polite \"you\"."],"rows":[["I","main","main"],["you (very close)","tu","too"],["you (friendly)","tum","toom"],["you (polite)","aap","aap"],["he / she / it","vah (woh)","woh"],["this (he / she / it, near)","yeh","yeh"],["we","hum","hoom"],["they","ve (woh)","woh"]],"ex":[["I am a student","main vidyaarthi hoon","main vid-YAAR-thee hoon"],["you are tall","tum lambe ho","toom LUM-beh hoh"],["she is my sister","vah meri behen hai","woh MEH-ree BAY-hen hai"],["we are friends","hum dost hain","hoom dohst hain"],["they are teachers","ve adhyaapak hain","woh uh-DHYAA-puk hain"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Masculine ending -aa becomes -e (ladkaa → ladke). Feminine -ee or -i becomes -iyaan (ladki → ladkiyaan), other feminine nouns add -en (kitaab → kitaaben). Many masculine nouns do not change (ghar)."],"rows":[["masculine -aa","ladkaa → ladke","LUD-kaa → LUD-keh"],["masculine (no change)","ghar → ghar","gur"],["feminine -ee","ladki → ladkiyaan","LUD-kee → LUD-kee-yaan"],["feminine","kitaab → kitaaben","ki-TAAB → ki-TAA-ben"],["feminine","aurat → auraten","OW-rut → OW-ru-ten"]],"ex":[["one boy, boys","ladkaa, ladke","LUD-kaa LUD-keh"],["one girl, girls","ladki, ladkiyaan","LUD-kee LUD-kee-yaan"],["one book, books","kitaab, kitaaben","ki-TAAB ki-TAA-ben"],["one house, houses","ghar, ghar","gur gur"],["one room, rooms","kamra, kamre","KUM-raa KUM-reh"]]},{"id":"hona-to-be","title":"Hona: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","main hoon","main hoon"],["you are (friendly)","tum ho","toom hoh"],["you are (polite)","aap hain","aap hain"],["he / she is","vah hai","woh hai"],["we are","hum hain","hoom hain"],["they are","ve hain","woh hain"]],"ex":[["I am English","main angrez hoon","main un-GRAYZ hoon"],["he is a doctor","vah doctor hai","woh DOK-tur hai"],["we are tired","hum thake hue hain","hoom THUH-keh hoo-EH hain"],["are you from Delhi?","kya aap Dilli se hain?","kyaa aap DIL-lee seh hain"],["they are at home","ve ghar par hain","woh gur pur hain"]]},{"id":"to-have-mere-paas","title":"To have (mere paas)","text":["Hindi says \"near me there is\": mere paas... hai. For family: mere... hain."],"rows":[["I have","mere paas hai","MEH-reh paas hai"],["you have (friendly)","tumhaare paas hai","toom-HAA-reh paas hai"],["you have (polite)","aapke paas hai","AAP-keh paas hai"],["he / she has","uske paas hai","OOS-keh paas hai"],["we have","hamaare paas hai","hum-AA-reh paas hai"],["they have","unke paas hai","OON-keh paas hai"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","mera ek bhai hai","MEH-raa ayk bhai hai"],["she has two cats","uske paas do billiyaan hain","OOS-keh paas doh BIL-lee-yaan hain"],["we have time","hamaare paas samay hai","hum-AA-reh paas SUM-ay hai"],["do you have a pen?","kya aapke paas kalam hai?","kyaa AAP-keh paas KUH-lum hai"],["they have a car","unke paas gaadi hai","OON-keh paas GAA-dee hai"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Take the stem (verb minus -naa) + -taa / -te / -tee + hona. Bolna (to speak), man speaking:"],"rows":[["main","bolta hoon","BOHL-taa hoon"],["tum","bolte ho","BOHL-teh hoh"],["aap","bolte hain","BOHL-teh hain"],["vah (m)","bolta hai","BOHL-taa hai"],["vah (f)","bolti hai","BOHL-tee hai"],["hum / ve","bolte hain","BOHL-teh hain"]],"ex":[["I work in a bank","main bank mein kaam karta hoon","main bunk mayn kaam KUR-taa hoon"],["you live in Delhi","tum Dilli mein rehte ho","toom DIL-lee mayn REH-teh hoh"],["she reads a book","vah kitaab padhti hai","woh ki-TAAB PUDH-tee hai"],["we learn Hindi","hum Hindi seekhte hain","hoom HIN-dee SEEKH-teh hain"],["they buy bread","ve roti khareedte hain","woh ROH-tee khu-REED-teh hain"]]},{"id":"jaana-to-go","title":"Jaana: to go","text":["Past: gaya (m), gayi (f), gaye (pl)."],"rows":[["I go","main jaata hoon","main JAA-taa hoon"],["you go (friendly)","tum jaate ho","toom JAA-teh hoh"],["you go (polite)","aap jaate hain","aap JAA-teh hain"],["he goes","vah jaata hai","woh JAA-taa hai"],["she goes","vah jaati hai","woh JAA-tee hai"],["we / they go","hum / ve jaate hain","hoom JAA-teh hain"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","main school jaata hoon","main skool JAA-taa hoon"],["where are you going?","aap kahaan jaa rahe hain?","aap ku-HAAN jaa RUH-heh hain"],["we are going home","hum ghar jaa rahe hain","hoom gur jaa RUH-heh hain"],["she is going shopping","vah kharidaari ke liye jaa rahi hai","woh khu-ree-DAA-ree keh LEE-yeh jaa RUH-hee hai"],["let's go!","chalo!","CHUH-loh"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Word order is subject, object, verb (the verb is last). Adjectives come before the noun."],"rows":[["subject + object + verb","Main roti khaata hoon.","main ROH-tee KHAA-taa hoon"],["adjective before noun","bada ghar","BUH-daa gur"],["add time or place","Main aaj yahaan kaam karta hoon.","main aaj yuh-HAAN kaam KUR-taa hoon"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","main roti khaata hoon","main ROH-tee KHAA-taa hoon"],["Anna reads a book","Anna kitaab padhti hai","AN-naa ki-TAAB PUDH-tee hai"],["we live in a big house","hum bade ghar mein rehte hain","hoom BUH-deh gur mayn REH-teh hain"],["he works here today","vah aaj yahaan kaam karta hai","woh aaj yuh-HAAN kaam KUR-taa hai"],["the dog is black","kutta kaala hai","KOOT-taa KAA-laa hai"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put nahin before the verb \"hona\" (or before the verb): main nahin jaata. In the present, nahin usually goes before the main verb."],"rows":[["not","nahin","nuh-HEEN"],["nothing","kuchh nahin","kooch nuh-HEEN"],["nobody","koi nahin","KOH-ee nuh-HEEN"],["never","kabhi nahin","KUB-hee nuh-HEEN"]],"ex":[]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Put kya at the start for a yes / no question, or raise your voice."],"rows":[["statement","Aap angrezi bolte hain.","aap un-gray-ZEE BOL-teh hain"],["question with kya","Kya aap angrezi bolte hain?","kyaa aap un-gray-ZEE BOL-teh hain"],["rising voice","Aap angrezi bolte hain?","aap un-gray-ZEE BOL-teh hain"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","kya aap angrezi bolte hain?","kyaa aap un-gray-ZEE BOL-teh hain"],["is she a doctor?","kya vah doctor hai?","kyaa woh DOK-tur hai"],["do you have a pen?","kya aapke paas kalam hai?","kyaa AAP-keh paas KUH-lum hai"],["are you tired?","kya aap thake hue hain?","kyaa aap THUH-keh hoo-EH hain"],["is it far?","kya yeh door hai?","kyaa yeh door hai"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","kya","kyaa"],["who","kaun","kown"],["where","kahaan","ku-HAAN"],["when","kab","kub"],["why","kyon","kyohn"],["how","kaise","KAI-seh"],["which","kaun sa","kown saa"],["how much / how many","kitna / kitne","KIT-naa / KIT-neh"]],"ex":[["what is this?","yeh kya hai?","yeh kyaa hai"],["who is she?","vah kaun hai?","woh kown hai"],["where do you live?","aap kahaan rehte hain?","aap ku-HAAN REH-teh hain"],["when is the exam?","pareeksha kab hai?","puh-REEK-shaa kub hai"],["why are you late?","aap der se kyon aaye?","aap dayr seh kyohn AA-yeh"],["how much is it?","yeh kitne ka hai?","yeh KIT-neh kaa hai"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":["Possessives agree with the thing owned: mera (m), meri (f), mere (pl m)."],"rows":[["my","mera / meri / mere","MEH-raa / MEH-ree / MEH-reh"],["your (friendly)","tumhaara / tumhaari","toom-HAA-raa"],["your (polite)","aapka / aapki","AAP-kaa / AAP-kee"],["his / her","uska / uski","OOS-kaa / OOS-kee"],["our","hamaara / hamaari","hum-AA-raa"],["their","unka / unki","OON-kaa / OON-kee"]],"ex":[["my house","mera ghar","MEH-raa gur"],["your friends","aapke dost","AAP-keh dohst"],["his sister","uski behen","OOS-kee BAY-hen"],["our teacher","hamaare adhyaapak","hum-AA-reh uh-DHYAA-puk"],["my mother","meri maa","MEH-ree maa"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["tu for children and very close friends. tum for friends. aap for strangers and elders. \"-ji\" after a name is respect (Sharma-ji). Hum is also used for \"I\" in very formal speech."],"rows":[["you, very close","tu","too"],["you, friendly","tum","toom"],["you, polite","aap","aap"],["respect after name","-ji","jee"]],"ex":[["come in (friendly)","aao","AA-oh"],["please come in (polite)","kripya aaiye","KRIP-yaa AA-ee-yeh"],["how are you? (friendly)","tum kaise ho?","toom KAI-seh hoh"],["how are you? (polite)","aap kaise hain?","aap KAI-seh hain"],["thank you, Mr Sharma","dhanyavaad, Sharma-ji","DHUN-yuh-vaad SHUR-maa-jee"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: verb stem + -aa / -ee / -e (agrees with the doer). Future: stem + -oongaa (m) / -oongee (f)."],"rows":[["I went (m)","main gaya","main GUH-yaa"],["I went (f)","main gayi","main GUH-yee"],["we went","hum gaye","hoom GUH-yeh"],["I will go (m)","main jaaoonga","main JAA-oon-gaa"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","kal maine kaam kiya","kul MAI-neh kaam KEE-yaa"],["she bought a book","usne kitaab khareedi","OOS-neh ki-TAAB khu-REE-dee"],["I went home","main ghar gaya","main gur GUH-yaa"],["I will call you tomorrow","main kal phone karoonga","main kul phohn kuh-ROON-gaa"],["we will eat at eight","hum aath baje khaayenge","hoom aath BUH-jeh KHAA-yen-geh"]]}],"name":"Hindi","id":"hi","flag":"in","script":"Devanagari","note":""}